    "title": "ISAAC - In Situ Animation of Accelerated Computations",
    "access_right": "open",
    "upload_type": "software",
    "license": "LGPL-3.0",
    "pub_id": "31686",
    "description": "Nowadays, many computationally intensive codes, such as those used for physics or biology simulations, are run on GPU-accelerated hardware. On large computing clusters, this hardware is distributed across multiple nodes, which communicate with each other via Message Passing Interface (MPI). The goal of ISAAC is to visualize this data without the need for expensive copy processes between accelerator and host. This allows ISAAC to fully take advantage of the high computation speed of these accelerators."
}
